# The pruning of the inner list of a dual list (D114) misses no pair within
# the cutoff, and the loop over pairs reaches every unit that holds one
# (D268). With MDIR_CHECK_PRUNING each step counts, at its own
# positions, the pairs within the cutoff in the outer list and in the inner
# one, the inner one through the active units that the loop takes; the
# runtime stops the run if the two differ, and reports the steps it checked.
# The run of pme-settle.test with an inner list of 9.3 Å pruned from an
# outer one of 11 Å, over several prunings between builds, in mixed and in
# double precision, and the mixture of argon and krypton of barostat.test
# under its barostat, whose cell changes at every step. Where the loop over
# pairs prunes for its refresh (D284, MDIR_FUSED_PRUNE=always),
# the check follows the loop, which writes the inner list.
#
# REQUIRES: cuda
#
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t
# RUN: cp %S/Inputs/opc/opc.prmtop %S/Inputs/opc/opc.inpcrd %S/Inputs/mixture.pdb %t
# RUN: sed -n '/^#--- run.toml/,/^#--- end/p' %S/pme-settle.test | sed '1d;$d' \
# RUN:     | sed -e 's|energy_interval = 50|energy_interval = 100|' -e 's|^steps *= 100|steps = 300|' \
# RUN:           -e 's|^pairlist_distance = 10.0|pairlist_distance = 11.0\npruned_distance = 9.3|' \
# RUN:           -e 's|^type = "PERIODIC"|type = "PERIODIC"\n[execution]\ntarget = "gpu"\nprecision = "mixed"\nneighbor_structure = "GROUPS"|' > %t/mixed.toml
# RUN: sed -e 's|^precision = "mixed"|precision = "double"|' %t/mixed.toml > %t/double.toml
# RUN: cd %t && env MDIR_CHECK_PRUNING=1 MDIR_COMPILE_CACHE=off mdir run mixed.toml > mixed.out 2> mixed.err
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=PRUNED < %t/mixed.out
# RUN: FileCheck %s < %t/mixed.err
# RUN: cd %t && env MDIR_CHECK_PRUNING=1 MDIR_COMPILE_CACHE=off mdir run double.toml > double.out 2> double.err
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=PRUNED < %t/double.out
# RUN: FileCheck %s < %t/double.err
# RUN: sed -n '/^#--- run.toml/,/^#--- end/p' %S/barostat.test | sed '1d;$d' \
# RUN:     | sed -e 's|energy_interval = 1000|energy_interval = 100|' -e 's|^steps *= 2000|steps = 300|' \
# RUN:           -e 's|^pairlist_distance = 10.0|pairlist_distance = 10.6\npruned_distance = 9.3|' > %t/npt.toml
# RUN: printf '[execution]\ntarget = "gpu"\nprecision = "mixed"\nneighbor_structure = "GROUPS"\n' >> %t/npt.toml
# RUN: cd %t && env MDIR_CHECK_PRUNING=1 MDIR_COMPILE_CACHE=off mdir run npt.toml > npt.out 2> npt.err
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=PRUNED < %t/npt.out
# RUN: FileCheck %s < %t/npt.err
# RUN: cd %t && env MDIR_FUSED_PRUNE=always MDIR_CHECK_PRUNING=1 MDIR_COMPILE_CACHE=off mdir run mixed.toml > fused.out 2> fused.err
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=PRUNED < %t/fused.out
# RUN: FileCheck %s < %t/fused.err
# RUN: cd %t && env MDIR_FUSED_PRUNE=always MDIR_CHECK_PRUNING=1 MDIR_COMPILE_CACHE=off mdir run double.toml > fused-double.out 2> fused-double.err
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=PRUNED < %t/fused-double.out
# RUN: FileCheck %s < %t/fused-double.err
# RUN: cd %t && env MDIR_FUSED_PRUNE=always MDIR_CHECK_PRUNING=1 MDIR_COMPILE_CACHE=off mdir run npt.toml > fused-npt.out 2> fused-npt.err
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=PRUNED < %t/fused-npt.out
# RUN: FileCheck %s < %t/fused-npt.err
# Without the variable the run checks nothing.
# RUN: cd %t && env MDIR_COMPILE_CACHE=off mdir run mixed.toml > plain.out 2>&1
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=PLAIN < %t/plain.out

# PRUNED:    MDIR: the inner lists were pruned {{[0-9]+}} times

# CHECK:     mdrt: the inner lists were checked at 30{{[01]}} steps: {{[1-9][0-9]+}} pairs within the cutoff, none missed

# PLAIN:     MDIR: the inner lists were pruned
# PLAIN-NOT: mdrt: the inner lists were checked
